From 621174e2a34f4eacedf0f0c27b59ee05b0b8bb4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 15:53:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] qos: Hardware QoS v2 - classful upload (qos_type=11)

Per-class hardware upload QoS on the Runner egress TM, keeping the flow
accelerator ON. Reuses the Traditional QoS classification engine
unmodified: add_qos_rules() CONNMARK classes land in skb->mark bits
[2:0], which are the Broadcom SKBMARK queue field (bcm_skb_defines.h)
that the flow cache copies into the Runner flow entry at flow creation,
steering accelerated flows into per-class WAN egress queues
(class N -> qid N; unclassified -> qid 0; LAN/mcast class -> qid 6).

start_hwqos_classful() programs PI2 AQM on qids 0-6 plus per-queue
shaper caps from the qos_orates class ceil percentages of qos_obw
(qid 0/6 capped at full OBW). No port-aggregate shaper exists in the
egress TM, so the GUI note tells users to keep ceils summing ~100%
for a strict total cap.

- shared.h: IS_HWQOS_CLASSFUL() (qos_enable=1 && qos_type=11)
- init-broadcom.c: classful exempted from fc_disable/runner_disable
- qos.c: add_iQosRules dispatches classful -> add_qos_rules (rules
  regenerate with every firewall mangle rebuild, so they survive
  service restarts); start_iQos -> start_hwqos_classful()
- rc.h: prototype
- QoS_EZQoS.asp: radio value 11 below the v1 radio (same hwqos_support
  gate), upload-only validation shared with type 10, classful desc
  note, engine-switch lands on the T.QoS rules editor

Steering mechanism verified against source (SKBMARK_GET_Q consumers in
rdpa_mw_blog_parse.c); on-metal probe showed CLASSIFY/skb->priority is
NOT honored on this platform, hence the mark-bits design. On-device
validation pending: per-queue counters, SP service order across qids,
and cap accuracy under load.
